      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Principles Before Personalities, back to top">
        <img src="assets/icon-64.png" width="28" height="28" alt="">
        <span>Principles Before Personalities</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#features">Features</a></li>
          <li><a href="#inside">What's inside</a></li>
          <li><a class="nav-cta" href="#download">Download</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="wrap hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Offline reader &amp; study companion</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Principles Before Personalities</h1>
          <p class="lede">A quiet, distraction-free reader for the <strong>public-domain 1939 first edition</strong> of <cite>Alcoholics Anonymous</cite>, with the page numbers read in meetings. Highlight, bookmark, leave sticky notes and search, all kept privately on your own device.</p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#download">Download</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#features">See what it does</a>
          </div>
          <ul class="chips" aria-label="At a glance">
            <li>No account</li>
            <li>Works offline</li>
            <li>Mac · Windows · Android · iPhone</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-art">
          <picture>
            <source srcset="assets/icon-320.webp" type="image/webp">
            <img src="assets/icon-320.png" width="320" height="320" alt="Principles Before Personalities app icon: a navy book with a glowing cyan bookmark ribbon">
          </picture>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="shot" aria-label="Screenshot">
      <div class="wrap">
        <figure>
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="assets/screenshot-reader-1200.webp 1200w, assets/screenshot-reader-2000.webp 2000w" sizes="(min-width: 1180px) 1100px, 94vw">
            <img src="assets/screenshot-reader-1200.jpg" srcset="assets/screenshot-reader-1200.jpg 1200w, assets/screenshot-reader-2000.jpg 2000w" sizes="(min-width: 1180px) 1100px, 94vw" width="1200" height="713" alt="Screenshot of the Mac app. A library sidebar lists the chapters of Alcoholics Anonymous with their page numbers. The reading sheet shows Chapter 7, Working With Others, on page 89, with a highlighter color tray, bookmark and sticky-note buttons and a find-in-book field in the toolbar, and page navigation at the bottom." decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
          </picture>
          <figcaption>The Mac app, open at Chapter 7, “Working With Others,” page 89. Actual screenshot.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <h2 id="about-title">What it is</h2>
        <p>Principles Before Personalities is a reader built for people who actually <em>work</em> the book. You get the 1939 text with its real page numbers, laid out as a warm paper page on a calm dark background, plus the tools you would use with a pen and a pad of sticky notes. Your highlights, bookmarks, notes and place are saved on your device. There is no account and nothing is uploaded.</p>
        <p>The name comes from the recovery tradition of placing “principles before personalities.”</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="features-title">Features</h2>
        <ul class="grid features">
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Two-pane reader</h3>
            <p>A library sidebar with collapsible books, parts and chapters sits beside a paper-style reading sheet.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Real page numbers</h3>
            <p>The text is split into the book's real pages. Type a page number to jump straight to it. <i>Bill's Story</i> starts on page 1 and <i>How It Works</i> on page 58.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Five-color highlighter</h3>
            <p>Select text and paint it in <span class="sw sw-yellow"></span>yellow, <span class="sw sw-amber"></span>amber, <span class="sw sw-pink"></span>pink, <span class="sw sw-green"></span>green or <span class="sw sw-blue"></span>blue. Overlapping highlights merge and split cleanly, and an eraser removes them.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Marked pages</h3>
            <p>Flag any page with a colored ribbon. A “Marked pages” list in the sidebar takes you back to each one.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Sticky notes</h3>
            <p>Drop a note on any page, then drag it, resize it and pick one of five colors. Chapters that contain notes show a small indicator in the sidebar.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Full-text search</h3>
            <p>Search the whole book, see the number of hits, step to the next or previous match, and find the current match marked on the page.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Easy navigation</h3>
            <p>Move by page or by chapter, and filter the chapter list by name to find a chapter quickly.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Import your own text</h3>
            <p>Open any <code>.txt</code> or <code>.md</code> file. It is split into chapters and pages automatically and added to your library, ready to highlight and annotate.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="card">
            <h3>Private and offline</h3>
            <p>No account, no network and no telemetry. Your place, highlights, bookmarks, notes and imported texts are saved automatically on your device and come back the next time you open the app.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="shortcuts">
          <h3>Keyboard shortcuts on Mac</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt><kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>→</kbd></dt><dd>Previous / next page</dd></div>
            <div><dt><kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>M</kbd></dt><dd>Mark this page</dd></div>
            <div><dt><kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>G</kbd></dt><dd>Find next</dd></div>
            <div><dt><kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>O</kbd></dt><dd>Import a text</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="inside" aria-labelledby="inside-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="inside-title">What's inside</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">The app comes with two texts. Both are from the <strong>1939 first edition</strong>, which is in the public domain in the United States. This is <strong>not</strong> the current fourth edition, and stories added in later editions are not included.</p>
        <div class="grid two">
          <article class="card paper">
            <h3><cite>Alcoholics Anonymous</cite></h3>
            <p class="sub">The basic text</p>
            <p>The Big Book as read in meetings, with meeting page numbers kept, from <i>Bill's Story</i> on page 1 through page 164.</p>
            <ul class="ticks">
              <li><strong>Front matter:</strong> the 1939 Foreword and The Doctor's Opinion</li>
              <li><strong>The Book:</strong> Bill's Story, There Is a Solution, More About Alcoholism, We Agnostics, How It Works, Into Action, Working With Others, To Wives, The Family Afterward, To Employers, A Vision for You</li>
              <li><strong>Appendix:</strong> Spiritual Experience</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="card paper">
            <h3>Personal Stories</h3>
            <p class="sub">First edition, 1939</p>
            <p>All 30 personal stories from the 1939 first edition, including The Doctor's Nightmare, The Unbeliever, The European Drinker, A Feminine Victory, Our Southern Friend and A Business Man's Recovery.</p>
            <p>You can add your own texts alongside them with <em>Import a text</em>.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt" id="download" aria-labelledby="download-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="download-title">Download</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">Choose your platform. Each download is a <code>.zip</code> file. The apps aren't distributed through an app store, so your device may ask you to confirm the first time. The steps for each platform are below.</p>
        <div class="grid downloads">
          <article class="card dl" aria-labelledby="dl-mac">
            <h3 id="dl-mac">Mac</h3>
            <p class="req">Native app · macOS 14 Sonoma or later</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="downloads/Principles-Before-Personalities-Mac.zip" download>Download for Mac</a>
            <ol>
              <li>Double-click the zip to unzip it (Safari may already have done this), then drag <b>Principles Before Personalities</b> into your Applications folder.</li>
              <li>The first time, Control-click (or right-click) the app, choose <b>Open</b>, then click <b>Open</b> again.</li>
              <li>If macOS still blocks it, go to <b>System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security</b> and click <b>Open Anyway</b>.</li>
            </ol>
          </article>
          <article class="card dl" aria-labelledby="dl-win">
            <h3 id="dl-win">Windows</h3>
            <p class="req">Desktop app · Windows 10 or Windows 11 (64-bit) · nothing else to install</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="downloads/Principles-Before-Personalities-Windows.zip" download>Download for Windows</a>
            <ol>
              <li>Right-click the zip, choose <b>Extract All</b>, and open the extracted <b>Principles Before Personalities</b> folder.</li>
              <li>Double-click <b>Principles Before Personalities.exe</b>. Keep the files in that folder together.</li>
              <li>If Microsoft Defender SmartScreen appears, click <b>More info</b>, then <b>Run anyway</b>.</li>
            </ol>
          </article>
          <article class="card dl" aria-labelledby="dl-android">
            <h3 id="dl-android">Android</h3>
            <p class="req">Installable app (<code>.apk</code>) · sideloaded</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="downloads/Principles-Before-Personalities-Android.zip" download>Download for Android</a>
            <ol>
              <li>Open the zip in your Files app and extract the <code>.apk</code>.</li>
              <li>Tap the <code>.apk</code>. When asked, allow <b>Install unknown apps</b> for the app you're installing from, then go back.</li>
              <li>Tap <b>Install</b>. If Google Play Protect shows a warning, you can choose to install anyway.</li>
            </ol>
          </article>
          <article class="card dl" aria-labelledby="dl-iphone">
            <h3 id="dl-iphone">iPhone</h3>
            <p class="req">Installable web app, <strong>not</strong> an App Store app</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="downloads/Principles-Before-Personalities-iPhone.zip" download>Download for iPhone</a>
            <ol>
              <li>The iPhone version is a web app that you add to your Home Screen. It has the same books and reading tools.</li>
              <li>Open the web app in <b>Safari</b>.</li>
              <li>Tap <b>Share</b>, then <b>Add to Home Screen</b>. It then opens from its own icon like an app.</li>
            </ol>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <h2 id="faq-title">Questions</h2>
        <details>
          <summary>Is this the current edition of the Big Book?</summary>
          <p>No. The app contains the 1939 first edition, which is in the public domain in the United States. It is not the current fourth edition, and stories added in later editions are not included.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is this an official Alcoholics Anonymous app?</summary>
          <p>No. Principles Before Personalities is an independent project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Alcoholics Anonymous World Services, Inc.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where are my highlights and notes stored?</summary>
          <p>Only on your own device. The app has no account and doesn't need a network connection. Nothing you read or write is uploaded.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Why is the iPhone version a web app?</summary>
          <p>Publishing a native app on the App Store requires Apple's paid Developer Program, so the iPhone version is an installable web app that you add to your Home Screen from Safari. It is not a native App Store app.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="disclaimer">Principles Before Personalities is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or approved by Alcoholics Anonymous World Services, Inc. The bundled text is the 1939 first edition of <cite>Alcoholics Anonymous</cite>, which is in the public domain in the United States.</p>
